# Environment variables and secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.development
# ...but DO track the template so new contributors can copy it
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*credentials*.json
*config.json
*secrets*.json
# 2026-08-10: `*config.json` above is meant for credential-bearing configs
# (firebase-config.json and friends). It also swallowed tsconfig.json, so CI
# checked out a tree with no TypeScript config — `npx tsc --noEmit` found no
# inputs, printed its help text and exited 1. The landing workflow had been red
# for days because of it. tsconfig.json holds compiler options only, no secrets.
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.*.json

# Sensitive files
**/*ISSUE*.png
**/*issue*.png
**/*TODO*.md
**/*todo*.md
**/ORCHESTRATOR_LOG.md
